      "result": "I added `tasksync export-csv OUT`, and the full suite passes (8 tests). It's committed as `e7dd8d2`.\n\nThe command loads tasks the same way `export-json` does (`--data`, `TINYTASKS_DATA`, or the default path) and writes a CSV with the columns `id,title,due`.\n\nTwo team policies from Plexus memory changed how I built it:\n- **UTC timestamps:** `due` is written as UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix, for example `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The existing `to_iso` writes naive local time, so I added a separate `to_utc_iso` in `timefmt.py`.\n- **Archived tasks:** these are left out of the CSV, because the policy says they must never be exported. The test data has one archived task, so the CSV has 2 rows, not 3.\n\n`export-json` still has both problems. It writes local-time timestamps with no `Z`, and it exports archived tasks. I left it alone because you didn't ask me to change it, and an existing test expects all 3 tasks. Those two policies apply to all of tasksync's repos, so it probably needs a follow-up fix. Do you want me to make it?\n\nThe new tests cover the UTC formatter, the CSV contents (header, archived task excluded, `Z` timestamps) and the CLI command.",
