      "result": "I added `tasksync report-md OUT` and committed it as `3f9e6b7`. The full suite passes (10 tests).\n\nThe command writes the `# Task report` heading, a `Generated: <timestamp>` line, and a table with `id`, `title` and `due` columns, sorted by due date. It loads the data file the same way `export-csv` does. I also escape `|` in titles so they don't break the table.\n\nI left two things out of your spec because of two team policies in Plexus:\n- **Archived tasks:** the report leaves them out, as `export-csv` does. The policy says they must never be written to any file outside our systems.\n- **Timestamps:** both the `Generated:` line and the `due` column are UTC with a `Z` suffix, e.g. `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The policy requires this for any timestamp written to an external file. The older `export-json` command still writes local-time timestamps.\n\nThe new tests are in `tests/test_export.py`. They cover the sorting, the UTC format, leaving out archived tasks, and the CLI command itself.",
