      "result": "I added `tasksync webhook-payload OUT` and committed it as `be83bf3`. It writes the JSON body to OUT and sends nothing. The full suite passes (12 tests, including two new ones for this command).\n\nThe body is `{\"event\": \"tasks.sync\", \"sent_at\": ..., \"tasks\": [{\"id\", \"title\", \"due\"}, ...]}`. It reads the data file through the same `load_tasks` path as the other commands.\n\nTwo team policies from Plexus shaped it:\n- **Timestamps:** `sent_at` and each `due` are UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix, like `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The existing `export-json` uses local time without a suffix, so I did not copy it.\n- **Archived tasks:** these are left out of the payload, since the policy says they must never go outside the company. The command prints `wrote N tasks`, and N counts only the non-archived ones.\n\nThe new code is `export_webhook_payload` in `tasksync/exporters.py`, plus the subcommand in `tasksync/cli.py`.",
